&lt;div id=&#34;welcome-to-module-4&#34; class=&#34;section level2&#34;&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Welcome to module 4&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Now that we can look at penguin data and visualise them, it’s time to &lt;em&gt;summarise&lt;/em&gt; our data numerically.&lt;br /&gt;
Descriptive statistics help us answer questions like:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;What’s a “typical” value?&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How much do values vary (differ)?&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How confident are we about the average value of our sample? Does it accurately reflect the population?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Think of this as learning the language of the data before asking bigger questions.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
